@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Usage insights and the privacy setting";
    var canConnect = ViewData["CanConnectUsageInsights"] is true;
}

<h1>Usage insights and the privacy setting</h1>

<p class="lead">Usage insights use a <strong>separate application</strong>,
<strong>MLCP Usage Insights</strong>, with one permission: <strong>Read all usage reports</strong>.
It is not part of connecting your organisation, and removing it never affects the main
connection.</p>

<h2 class="h5">Turning it on</h2>
<ol>
    <li>Connect your organisation first.</li>
    <li>A Global Administrator or Privileged Role Administrator selects
        <strong>Connect MLCP Usage Insights</strong> below or on the connection status page.</li>
    <li>Microsoft's consent screen shows the application <strong>MLCP Usage Insights</strong> and the
        single permission it asks for. Accept it.</li>
    <li>Your organisation will then list two enterprise applications: <strong>MLCP</strong> and
        <strong>MLCP Usage Insights</strong>. To turn usage insights off later, remove only the
        second one.</li>
</ol>

@if (canConnect)
{
    <form asp-controller="Onboarding" asp-action="ConnectUsageInsights" method="post" class="mb-4">
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Connect MLCP Usage Insights</button>
    </form>
}

<h2 class="h5">The privacy setting</h2>

<p>
    By default Microsoft hides user names in usage reports. We can show <strong>how many</strong>
    licensed users are active per service without changing anything at all.
</p>

<div class="alert alert-warning" role="note">
    To see <strong>which</strong> users or departments are inactive, an administrator must turn off
    <em>Display concealed user, group, and site names in all reports</em> in
    <strong>Microsoft 365 admin centre &rarr; Settings &rarr; Org settings &rarr; Reports</strong>.
    That changes what every administrator in your organisation sees in Microsoft's own reports too,
    not just here.
</div>

<p class="text-muted">
    MLCP will never change this setting for you. We record only that you told us you had changed
    it, and you can tell us to stop using identifiable names at any time.
</p>

<a class="btn btn-primary" asp-controller="Onboarding" asp-action="Index">Back to connection status</a>
